   o The common answer was "savecore -c" (which worked beautifully) to mark
     the dump invalid without copying it.

   o The second answer (which we may use - I suspect this problem will be
     with us for a while) is to use "/usr/sbin/rcmgr set SAVECORE_FLAGS M".
     It's also possible to change the dump directory to something other
     than /var/adm/crash ...
     
   The notes about the "rcmgr" approach conflicted a bit - one indicated it
   would prevent the system from creating core dump files, another said it
   would keep the system from going into single-user mode if a core dump
   could not be written.  Another look in our /etc/rc.config shows that we
   don't have an entry for SAVECORE_FLAGS, but I'm not sure it's a problem.

