Well, I got quite a few answers, all of them veryfying that it
works. A few fellas sent me pieces of their config files,
and by looking at these I was able to make a config file by hand.
And it worked! This is what it requires:

bus             tcds1      at tc0       slot  0 vector    tcdsintr
controller      asc1       at tcds1     slot  0 vector    ascintr
controller      asc2       at tcds1     slot  1 vector    ascintr

My card was in slot 0, I guess thats where the 'tc0' comes from. 
Some people already had a 2nd scsicontroller that of course changes
the tcds & asc numbering.

I still don't know why genvmunix didn't recognize the board,
(I doublechecked that I had the right genvmunix etc). But
this works ok for me.

