From tru64-unix-managers  Sat Feb 04 05:33:41 1995
From: Dan Jacobson <danj () gdb ! org>
Date: Sat, 04 Feb 1995 05:33:41 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary - .forward file
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075317506380



I received two quick responses this evening to the mystery of the reticent
.forward files.  Neither one had the correct answer but they got me
thinking in the right direction :-).  It turns out the the two
non-functional .forward files had permissions 755, while the one that
worked had permissions 644.  Changing the permissions of all .forward
files to 644 did the trick - they all work now.  This would seem a bit
counter-intuitive to me (giving a file 'more' permission causes it to
'break'???) - but it works.

Thanks to all for a quick response and a problem solved.

Cheers,

Dan Jacobson

