From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Nov 12 09:52:29 1998
From: Daniel David Benson <bensond () ssds ! ucdavis ! edu>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 1998 09:52:29 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: DECServer 700
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078728411866


Thanks to all who replied.  

Tom Webster <webster@ssdpdc.lgb.cal.boeing.com> nailed it for me.  I 
had the dip switches set wrong on my modems.  The DECserver was attempting
to send the hang command but the way I set the dip switches the modem
simply ignored it.  Oddly enough there is no way to turn off the automatic
hang up from the ASM software.  I didn't dig deep into the console 
commands.  It just seems to me that this should be an option.

Thanks!

-Dan


